.TH LAIN 6 "November 2026" "re:Lain 0.2.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
lain \- native client for the Serial Experiments Lain PlayStation game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lain
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lain
is a native Linux client built from the PlayStation game decompilation.
It runs the ported game code directly and does not use a PlayStation emulator.
The program includes a graphical launcher for importing game discs,
configuring the display, and managing optional subtitles and mods.
.PP
No copyrighted game data is installed by this package. A personal dump of
the original PlayStation discs is required.
.SH GETTING STARTED
Obtain raw Redump-format disc images of the two original PlayStation discs,
in CUE/BIN format. Launch
.B lain
and import Disc 1 and Disc 2 from the graphical launcher's disc picker.
Then select
.B Play
to start the game.
.PP
The importer requires raw 2352-byte-per-sector BIN/IMG data tracks.
CHD and 2048-byte/sector ISO images are not supported.
.SH CONTROLS
The default desktop controls include:
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Move the cursor or select a node (PlayStation D-pad).
.TP
.B V
Confirm/open a node (circle).
.TP
.B C
Go back (cross).
.TP
.B Z
Open the in-game menu (triangle).
.TP
.B Return
Continue or skip (Start).
.TP
.B F1
Open the in-game client options menu.
.PP
Physical gamepads are supported. Bindings can be adjusted in the application.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A desktop with OpenGL 3.2, SDL2, and OpenAL is required. Game data must be
supplied separately from personally obtained original disc dumps.
.SH FILES
The launcher manages imported disc data, saves, settings, and modifications
within the user's account. See the installed PORTING.md and MODDING.md
documentation for further details.
